  description: Asteroids are rocky or metallic objects that orbit the Sun and are
    remnants of the early Solar System. Most known asteroids are found in the main
    asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter, although many travel in other regions
    of the Solar System.
  interestingFact: Asteroids vary greatly in size, from small rocky fragments to
    objects hundreds of kilometers across.
